<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>com.convivy.ip-forwarding</string>
  <!-- Re-enable IPv4/IPv6 forwarding at boot so the mini's Tailscale exit node
       keeps routing across reboots (sysctl -w is otherwise lost on restart).

       NOTE: this is a system LaunchDaemon (needs root to set sysctl), UNLIKE the
       com.convivy.* files here, which are user LaunchAgents. Install it into the
       SYSTEM domain, not gui/$uid:
         sudo cp com.convivy.ip-forwarding.plist /Library/LaunchDaemons/
         sudo chown root:wheel /Library/LaunchDaemons/com.convivy.ip-forwarding.plist
         sudo launchctl bootstrap system /Library/LaunchDaemons/com.convivy.ip-forwarding.plist
       It is RunAtLoad-only (no KeepAlive): fires once at boot, sets forwarding,
       exits — so `launchctl print system/com.convivy.ip-forwarding` shows
       state=not running between boots, which is correct. Added for the mini
       exit-node work, 2026-07-02. -->
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/usr/sbin/sysctl</string>
    <string>-w</string>
    <string>net.inet.ip.forwarding=1</string>
    <string>net.inet6.ip6.forwarding=1</string>
  </array>
  <key>RunAtLoad</key>
  <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
